Cell["\<\
PASS means agreement at the numerical samples tested, not an analytic proof. \
Opp Sign means the nonzero residues consistently agree with opposite signs. \
FAIL means another disagreement was found. UNRESOLVED means a comparison \
could not be completed. To convert a channel to the physical residue, the \
checker multiplies its expression by -z and its selected PropDen, once. The \
minus follows from (i A_L)(i A_R)(i/PropDen)/i = -A_L A_R/PropDen. Neither \
the supplied channel rows nor the candidate amplitude is changed. \
Reload Setup and reevaluate the examples to update saved outputs. Keep Me \
and EE symbolic; ParameterRules below supplies their test values.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"84d972cc-6d04-4084-9f0b-fc6652521be4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Four-Point QED: e, E, e, E", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c2099370-ff2f-403e-8dfe-5035d48eca06"],

Cell["Load the QED three-point model (model 2) and generate the diagrams.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c411e5ee-c27c-415e-bce9-7d930f3981a9"],

Cell["\<\
qedDiagramModel = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"models\"}], 2];
fourPointParticles = {\"e\", \"E\", \"e\", \"E\"};
fourPointDiagrams = CreateDiagrams[fourPointParticles, qedDiagramModel];
CreateArrowDiagrams[fourPointDiagrams];\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0014998503141403`*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[66]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c86b6186-78eb-40ef-9be2-65b3cff5e0f3"],

Cell["\<\
Calculate their amplitudes and get the factorization channels from the same \
model. These are the ordinary channels: each contains its pole and the \
product of lower-point amplitudes divided by the propagator denominator.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02a10b14-0491-4168-a588-6a047cf67561"],

Cell["\<\
fourPointDiagramAmplitudes = diagramAmplitudes[fourPointDiagrams];
fourPointChannels = FactorizationAmplitudeChannels[
  fourPointParticles, qedDiagramModel];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[70]:=",ExpressionUUID->"15b97540-772e-41e1-9199-36ee4086f886"],

Cell["\<\
Pass those results and the model to the checker. Its normal output is just \
the channel, exchanged mass and result.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cfd8503a-f834-4dd2-81f4-9d4eb85edabe"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
CheckPhysicalResidues[
  fourPointDiagramAmplitudes, fourPointChannels, qedDiagramModel,
  \"ParameterRules\" -> {Me -> 1, EE -> 1}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[72]:=",ExpressionUUID->"fab001d3-19f8-41e5-a190-c77a346195d3"],

