Cell["\<\
Expected: two PASS rows, one for each physical pole. After converting each \
channel product to a physical residue with the sewing minus sign, it agrees \
with the cubic diagrams. An Opp Sign result remains available for a candidate \
with the opposite sign.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d1219e6c-cec0-4068-afeb-15c38ec69b17"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Five-Point QED: e, E, A.+, A.+, A.+", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3fb4c36c-426d-46f0-ab62-cb192953bd33"],

Cell["\<\
Load the existing QED model with three- and four-point amplitudes (model 3) \
for five-point factorization. Continue using the three-point model (model 2) \
to generate diagrams.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b5e5613e-98e5-4ca2-9d40-bb7d672b76a9"],

Cell["\<\
qedFactorizationModel = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \
\"models\"}], 3];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[73]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cde29785-488c-4cd5-87e9-56805c7c59dc"],

Cell["Generate the six diagrams in the usual way.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fea111d3-f86b-4d8f-82c5-292bfb3ef2aa"],

Cell["\<\
fivePointParticles = {\"e\", \"E\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\"};
fivePointDiagrams = CreateDiagrams[fivePointParticles, qedDiagramModel];
fivePointDiagramAmplitudes = diagramAmplitudes[fivePointDiagrams];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[74]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b85c76fd-6583-442b-835e-02ad7be84bc7"],

Cell["\<\
For this example, use a common reference spinor for all three photons. The \
replacement below gives every Xi the same label, 0. The original diagram \
amplitudes remain in fivePointDiagramAmplitudes.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2468670b-8963-43ca-8066-9cc79d018fa1"],

Cell["\<\
fivePointCheckAmplitudes = fivePointDiagramAmplitudes /.
  Spinor[\"Xi\", type_, _Integer] :> Spinor[\"Xi\", type, 0];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[77]:=",ExpressionUUID->"55c0aeca-5459-4318-bf83-48e8985f5c93"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Simplify Before Checking", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"51e2e9ed-bee3-4c18-afe6-ae21c7691d44"],

Cell["\<\
First contract the internal spin indices with each diagram's own mass rules. \
Then expand composite momenta inside spinor chains, using momentum \
conservation to choose the shorter sum, and reduce the individual chains. The \
original propagator denominators stay off shell and unchanged. No internal \
on-shell conditions are applied to the combined amplitude.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f23c42f7-2d3a-4be2-8fb2-2dac8f0b9774"],

Cell["\<\
fivePointRawAmplitude = Total[
  (ReduceSpinContractions[Last[#]] /. First[#]) & /@
    fivePointCheckAmplitudes];

fivePointSimplifyChain[chain_SpinorChain] := ReduceSpinorProducts[
  chain /. Mom[Multiparticle[labels__Integer]] :>
    With[{inside = {labels},
      outside = Complement[Range[Length[fivePointParticles]], {labels}]},
      If[Length[outside] < Length[inside],
        -Total[Mom /@ outside], Total[Mom /@ inside]]]];

fivePointSimplifiedDiagrams = Function[pair,
  {First[pair], Factor[
    (ReduceSpinContractions[Last[pair]] /. First[pair]) /.
      chain_SpinorChain :> fivePointSimplifyChain[chain]]}] /@
  fivePointCheckAmplitudes;
fivePointSimplifiedAmplitude = Total[Last /@ fivePointSimplifiedDiagrams];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[78]:=",ExpressionUUID->"15d3c886-e436-4b41-a221-abd724b9e403"],

Cell["\<\
This is a partial simplification: composite momenta have been removed from \
the spinor chains, but the common reference spinor Xi remains. The following \
cells show the actual calculated expression and its complexity, not a \
replacement by a known answer.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"046b9446-74b4-4c0f-a743-73a3550c0f20"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

